    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d836">

                <pb facs="1524" n="1490" sameAs="frus:frus1948v02/pg1490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.J/4–748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d836-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-07T23:00:00-05:00">April 7, 1948—11
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Martel 26. Personal for Lovett from Marshall. Reference Telmar 29<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d836-f2"/> regarding Austria: I am concerned lest we be put clearly
                    in position of thwarting conclusion of Austrian treaty. What are the odds
                    between general world effect of concluding treaty and risk of Soviet subversion
                    of government following withdrawal of troops?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d836-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d836-f1-content">
                <p>Secretary Marshall was at Bogotá attending the Ninth International Conference of
                    American States, March 30–May 2, 1948.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d836-f2" n="2" xml:id="d836-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it summarized paragraph 7 of Delsec 1658, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi> (710.J/4–648).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
